# .canon-owners — who owns what in this vault.
#
#   <glob>   <owner-email>[,<more>]   # comment
#
# Matched against repo-relative paths, first matching rule wins (like
# CODEOWNERS). A trailing /** or / covers everything beneath. Use * as the owner
# to mean "anyone", which is useful to carve an open subtree out of a governed
# parent.
#
# WHAT THIS IS: a local pre-commit warning, so an agent tidying the product
# vision gets told to propose instead. WHAT IT IS NOT: enforcement — it runs on
# the author's machine from a file the author can edit. Pair it with GitHub
# CODEOWNERS + a protected branch, which is the part that actually cannot be
# bypassed. See docs/MULTIPLAYER.md.
#
# Keep this list SHORT. Govern the few notes where being wrong is expensive;
# govern everything and people will route around you.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leadership-owned: direction, not documentation. Propose via PR.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vision/**                    lead@example.com

# The router is loaded into every agent's context on every session — a careless
# edit here changes how the whole team's agents behave.
Vision/Agent Router.md       lead@example.com,staff@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accepted decisions are the historical record. ADDING a new decision note is
# open to everyone; REWRITING an accepted one is not — that is how you quietly
# lose the reason a choice was made.
#
# This rule cannot distinguish "new file" from "edit" (both are staged changes),
# so it will warn on your own new decision notes too. If that friction annoys
# your team, delete this rule and rely on PR review for Decisions/ instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decisions/**               lead@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly open: the working layers. Everyone writes here, all the time.
# Listed for clarity even though unmatched paths are open by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sessions/**                  *
Projects/**                  *
Clients/**                   *
Reference/**                 *
Outputs/**                   *
Sources/**                   *
_Inbox/**                    *
